title: Capsley_Welcome
position: -825,-253
group: Capsley
---
<<declare $NPC_Variables_Name = "Ogbert">>
<<declare $player_gold = 10>>
<<declare $player_spoke_to_sally = false>>
<<enum Meal>>
  <<case None>>
  <<case Ramen>>
  <<case Pizza>>
  <<case MeatProduct>>
  <<case Sludge>>
<<endenum>>
<<declare $player_meal = Meal.None>>
<<declare $player_can_afford_bribe = $player_gold >= 6>>

Capsley: Hi! Welcome to Yarn Spinner! #line:Capsley_Welcome_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: This is the Feature Tour! #line:Capsley_Welcome_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: Walk through these rooms to learn about the major features of Yarn Spinner. #line:Capsley_Welcome_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: You can find me in each one. #line:Capsley_Welcome_0400_Capsley 
Capsley: I'll tell you what you're seeing in the room. #line:Capsley_Welcome_0500_Capsley 
Capsley: Or you can just be confused... #line:Capsley_Welcome_0600_Capsley 
Capsley: And wander alone. #line:Capsley_Welcome_0700_Capsley 
Capsley: Just like the real world. #line:Capsley_Welcome_0800_Capsley 
Capsley: Anyway... #line:Capsley_Welcome_0900_Capsley 
Capsley: Have a lovely day! #line:Capsley_Welcome_1000_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room2
position: -615,-253
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: Hello again. #line:Capsley_Room2_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: The characters in this room show off the main elements of writing dialogue in Yarn Spinner. #line:Capsley_Room2_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: Lines, options, nodes, and jumps. #line:Capsley_Room2_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: see you soon. #line:Capsley_Room2_0400_Capsley 
Capsley: really soon. #line:Capsley_Room2_0500_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room3
position: -825,-122
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: Well, well, well, if it isn't you. #line:Capsley_Room3_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: This room shows off detours! #line:Capsley_Room3_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: Which are similar to jumps... #line:Capsley_Room3_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: And are another way to structure your game! #line:Capsley_Room3_0400_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room4
position: -615,-122
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: Fancy seeing you here! #line:Capsley_Room4_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: This room shows off using variables in Yarn! #line:Capsley_Room4_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: And also shows off enumerations, or enums! #line:Capsley_Room4_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: Which are another type of variable! #line:Capsley_Room4_0400_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room5
position: -825,11
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: Oh, you're still here? #line:Capsley_Room5_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: Well then! I guess you want to see how to do conditionals and branching in Yarn. #line:Capsley_Room5_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: Which is what this room is all about, using ifs, onces, and options to do branching! #line:Capsley_Room5_0300_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room6
position: -615,11
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: You've almost reached the end. #line:Capsley_Room6_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: Here, we're showing off commands, functions, and smart variables. #line:Capsley_Room6_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: All of these are more advanced elements of Yarn Spinner to give you more control and hooks! #line:Capsley_Room6_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: Hooks both into Yarn, and hooks into the other parts of your game! #line:Capsley_Room6_0400_Capsley 
===
title: Capsley_Room7
position: -825,143
group: Capsley
---
Capsley: The final room, or is it? #line:Capsley_Room7_0100_Capsley 
Capsley: Nah, it is. #line:Capsley_Room7_0200_Capsley 
Capsley: This room demonstrates storylets, which are a new way of organising story content. #line:Capsley_Room7_0300_Capsley 
Capsley: Here, we show off two variants of storylets: line groups, and node groups. #line:Capsley_Room7_0400_Capsley 
===

title: Room2_Nodes_and_Lines
group: Room2
position: -305,-245
---
Bob: Hello. I'm Bob. #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0100_Bob 
Bob: I'm talking to you from my very own node. #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0200_Bob 
Bob: Each of these lines... #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0300_Bob 
Bob: ... is a line! #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0400_Bob 
Bob: Yarn Spinner scripts are made up of Nodes and Lines. #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0500_Bob 
Bob: Neat, huh? #line:Room2_Nodes_and_Lines_0600_Bob 
===

title: Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1
group: Room2
position: -42,-248
---
Bill: Hello. I'm Bill. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0100_Bill 
    -> Hi, I'm The Player. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0200 
    -> Hello, Bill. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0300 
Bill: See those choices you just had?  #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0400_Bill 
Bill: Those are called Options. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0500_Bill 
Bill: They let you create lines in your nodes that offer players, like you, a choice. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0600_Bill 
    -> That's pretty neat! #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0700 
        Bill: It is neat! #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0800_Bill 
        <<jump Room2_Options_and_Jumps_2>>
    -> OK... #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_1_0900 
        <<jump Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3>>
===

title: Room2_Options_and_Jumps_2
group: Room2
position: -247,-26
---
Bill: It's easy to move between nodes with Jump Commands. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_2_0100_Bill 
Bill: So easy, in fact, that we just did it without you even noticing. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_2_0200_Bill 
Bill: It's very neat! #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_2_0300_Bill 
===
title: Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3
group: Room2
position: 273,-142
---
Bill: You could be more enthusiastic. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3_0100_Bill 
Bill: Either way, we're in another node now. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3_0200_Bill 
Bill: We got here with a Jump Command. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3_0300_Bill 
Bill: Jump Commands let you move the dialogue between nodes. #line:Room2_Options_and_Jumps_3_0400_Bill 
===

title: Room3_Detours_1
group: Room3
position: -299,292
---
Bruce: I'm Bruce. My single purpose in life... #line:Room3_Detours_1_0100_Bruce 
Bruce: My raison d'être... #line:Room3_Detours_1_0200_Bruce 
Bruce: My whole reason to get up in the morning... #line:Room3_Detours_1_0300_Bruce 
Bruce: .. is to tell you about detours. #line:Room3_Detours_1_0400_Bruce 
<<detour Room3_Detours_2>>
Bruce: You'll end up back in the original node. #line:Room3_Detours_1_0500_Bruce 
Bruce: Like you are right now. SURPRISE! #line:Room3_Detours_1_0600_Bruce 
Bruce: Detours. Amazing.  #line:Room3_Detours_1_0700_Bruce 
Bruce: They work like Jump Commands, but bring you back at the end. #line:Room3_Detours_1_0800_Bruce 
Bruce: I don't actually get up in the morning, by the way. #line:Room3_Detours_1_0900_Bruce 
Bruce: I'm always here.  #line:Room3_Detours_1_1000_Bruce 
===

title: Room3_Detours_2
group: Room3
position: -244,538
---
Bruce: This is a detour. Right now. We just detoured to a whole different node. #line:Room3_Detours_2_0100_Bruce 
Bruce: Amazing, right? #line:Room3_Detours_2_0200_Bruce 
Bruce: And when we're done here... #line:Room3_Detours_2_0300_Bruce 
===

title: Room4_Variables_1
group: Room4
position: 168,589
---
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: Hi. I'm {$NPC_Variables_Name}. Or I can be someone else if you prefer? #line:Room4_Variables_1_0100_{0} 
    -> You're Arnold. #line:Room4_Variables_1_0200 
        <<set $NPC_Variables_Name = "Arnold">>
    -> Hmm... You're Terrence. #line:Room4_Variables_1_0300 
        <<set $NPC_Variables_Name = "Terrence">>
    -> Studley.  #line:Room4_Variables_1_0400 
        <<set $NPC_Variables_Name = "Studley">>
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: Easy done! #line:Room4_Variables_1_0500_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: That happened because of a Variable. #line:Room4_Variables_1_0600_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: My whole name is just a Variable. And it's set when you tell me who I am. #line:Room4_Variables_1_0700_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: You can update them or check them any time. #line:Room4_Variables_1_0800_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: Or use them in lines, like this... #line:Room4_Variables_1_0900_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: My name is {$NPC_Variables_Name}, and will always be {$NPC_Variables_Name}, until you change it. #line:Room4_Variables_1_1000_{0} 
{$NPC_Variables_Name}: How cool is that? #line:Room4_Variables_1_1100_{0} 
===

title: Room4_Variables_2
group: Room4
position: 153,407
---
Sally: Did you speak to {$NPC_Variables_Name}? #line:Room4_Variables_2_0100_Sally 
Sally: They left out the best bit of Variables! #line:Room4_Variables_2_0200_Sally 
Sally: They don't have to be strings of text. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0300_Sally 
Sally: They can also be numbers. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0400_Sally 
Sally: For example, you have {$player_gold} pieces of gold. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0500_Sally 
Sally: I know that because there's a Variable that tracks it. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0600_Sally 
Sally: I'm also setting a boolean variable that indicates you've spoken to me. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0700_Sally 
Sally: Booleans are just a fancy word for something that is true or false. #line:Room4_Variables_2_0800_Sally 
<<set $player_spoke_to_sally = true>>
Sally: Bye now! #line:Room4_Variables_2_0900_Sally 
===

title: Room5_IfStatements_1
group: Room5
position: 646,107
---
<<if $player_spoke_to_sally>>
    Mary: I know you spoke to Sally about Variables. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0100_Mary 
    Mary: I know because we're inside an if-statement that checks if that variable is true. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0200_Mary 
    Mary: AND IT IS TRUE! I KNOW! #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0300_Mary 
    Mary: Also I was watching you. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0400_Mary 
<<else>>
    Mary: You should try speaking to Sally in the previous room. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0500_Mary 
    Mary: I say this to everyone who hasn't spoken to her... #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0600_Mary 
    Mary: Because.. well.. these lines are inside the if and else statements. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0700_Mary 
    Mary: And you'll only see them if the condition on the if statement is not true. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0800_Mary 
    Mary: What's the condition, you ask? #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_0900_Mary 
    Mary: I'm not saying. Just go speak to Sally in the previous room. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_1000_Mary 
    Mary: Then come back to me. And maybe you'll figure it out. #line:Room5_IfStatements_1_1100_Mary 
<<endif>>
===

title: Room5_ConditionalOptions_1
group: Room5
position: 662,262
---
Thor: Hi.  #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0100_Thor 
    -> Hi, Thor. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0200 
        Thor: Hi. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0300_Thor 
    -> Hi, Thor. Do you know Sally? <<if $player_spoke_to_sally>> #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0400 
        Thor: Oh, yeah. I do. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0500_Thor 
        Thor: And you could only ask me that because that was a Conditional Option. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0600_Thor 
        Thor: A Conditional Option is like a regular Option... but it has a little if-statement attached to the end of its line. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0700_Thor 
        Thor: And that little if-statement... if it evaluates to true... then you get to see the option, and potentially choose it. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0800_Thor 
Thor: Toodles! Have a nice day. #line:Room5_ConditionalOptions_1_0900_Thor 
===

title: Room5_Enums_1
group: Room5
position: 668,438
---
Ruby: Would you like a meal? Ramen, Pizza, Nutritional Sludge(tm), or Meat Product? #line:Room5_Enums_1_0100_Ruby 
    -> Sure, Ramen please. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0200 
        <<set $player_meal = .Ramen>>
    -> Pizza. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0300 
        <<set $player_meal = .Pizza>>    
    -> Nutritional Sludge(tm) is my favourite! That one. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0400 
        <<set $player_meal = .Sludge>>
    -> ... Meat Product, I guess. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0500 
        <<set $player_meal = .MeatProduct>>   
Ruby: Neat! I just set an Enum to the meal you chose. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0600_Ruby 
Ruby: Enums are a special kind of variables, whose value is constrained to a predefined list of things. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0700_Ruby 
Ruby: Can you guess what the list of things might be? #line:Room5_Enums_1_0800_Ruby 
Ruby: That's right! It's the different meals I have for you! Or no meal. #line:Room5_Enums_1_0900_Ruby 
<<if $player_meal == .Ramen>>
    Ruby: Anyway... You got Ramen. #line:Room5_Enums_1_1000_Ruby 
    Ruby: That one is my favourite. #line:Room5_Enums_1_1100_Ruby 
    Ruby: And I'm telling you that because I used an if-statement to check which value of the Meal Enum is stored in the variable I'm using to track the player's meal. #line:Room5_Enums_1_1200_Ruby 
    Ruby: Works well, right? #line:Room5_Enums_1_1300_Ruby 
<<endif>>
Ruby: Bye bye! #line:Room5_Enums_1_1400_Ruby 
===

title: Room5_Once_1
group: Room5
position: 647,611
---
<<once>>
    Norb: Hi, I'm Norb. #line:Room5_Once_1_0100_Norb 
    Norb: I'm only ever going to talk to you ONCE! #line:Room5_Once_1_0200_Norb 
    Norb: Once and no more.  #line:Room5_Once_1_0300_Norb 
    Norb: Next time you speak to me I won't greet you. #line:Room5_Once_1_0400_Norb 
    Norb: That's because my greeting lines are inside a Once Statement. #line:Room5_Once_1_0500_Norb 
    Norb: Which.. well you can guess what it does. #line:Room5_Once_1_0600_Norb 
    Norb: Once statements can also be added to options, which means they can only be chosen once. #line:Room5_Once_1_0700_Norb 
    Norb: You can even put conditions on Once statements. #line:Room5_Once_1_0800_Norb 
<<endonce>>
===

title: Room6_Commands_1
group: Room6
position: 99,903
---
Derek: YOU! #line:Room6_Commands_1_0100_Derek 
    -> Me? #line:Room6_Commands_1_0200 
Derek: Yes, you! #line:Room6_Commands_1_0300_Derek 
<<wait 2>>
Derek: That was a dramatic pause, right? #line:Room6_Commands_1_0400_Derek 
Derek: I did that with a Command! The Wait Command! #line:Room6_Commands_1_0500_Derek 
Derek: You can make your own Commands to let Yarn Spinner Scripts control Godot Scripts. #line:Room6_Commands_1_0600_Derek 
Derek: So you can use them to make things happen in the game world, from Yarn Spinner. #line:Room6_Commands_1_0700_Derek 
Derek: The Wait Command comes with Yarn Spinner though. #line:Room6_Commands_1_0800_Derek 
Derek: Think of Commands like stage directions. #line:Room6_Commands_1_0900_Derek 
Derek: Anyway, bye! #line:Room6_Commands_1_1000_Derek 
===

title: Room6_Functions_1
group: Room6
position: 343,902
---
Beryl: Psst... #line:Room6_Functions_1_0100_Beryl 
    -> Yes? #line:Room6_Functions_1_0200 
Beryl: Wanna learn about Functions? #line:Room6_Functions_1_0300_Beryl 
    -> ... sure. #line:Room6_Functions_1_0400 
Beryl: Functions are things that provide a value to your Yarn Spinner Scripts. #line:Room6_Functions_1_0500_Beryl 
Beryl: For example... I can roll a dice, because Yarn Spinner provides a dice Function. #line:Room6_Functions_1_0600_Beryl 
<<if dice(6) == 6>>
    Beryl: I rolled a six! #line:Room6_Functions_1_0700_Beryl 
<<else>>
    Beryl: Well, I didn't roll a six. Alas. #line:Room6_Functions_1_0800_Beryl 
<<endif>>
Beryl: My favourite number, right at this moment, is {random_range(1,10)}! #line:Room6_Functions_1_0900_Beryl 
Beryl: But next time you ask me, it might be different. That's because I used the random_range function to get my favourite number. #line:Room6_Functions_1_1000_Beryl 
Beryl: I'm fickle as heck. #line:Room6_Functions_1_1100_Beryl 
Beryl: Anyway, Yarn Spinner has lots of built-in Functions. #line:Room6_Functions_1_1200_Beryl 
Beryl: But you can also make your own, to get information out of Godot Scripts. #line:Room6_Functions_1_1300_Beryl 
Beryl: Anyway, bye. #line:Room6_Functions_1_1400_Beryl 
===

title: Room6_SmartVariables_1
group: Room6
position: -147,906
---
Reginald: Did you know that Variables can also be Smart? #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0100_Reginald 
Reginald: When they're Smart, we call them Smart Variables. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0200_Reginald 
Reginald: We're proud of our evocative naming choices. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0300_Reginald 
<<if $player_can_afford_bribe>>
    Reginald: Anyway. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0400_Reginald 
    Reginald: I know you can afford to bribe me because you have enough gold. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0500_Reginald 
    <<set $player_gold = $player_gold - 6>>
    Reginald: And I know this because there's a Smart Variable that is set to true if the variable that tracks how much gold you have is greater than or equal to a certain value. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0600_Reginald 
    Reginald: Smart Variables let you simplify if-statements, and clarify dependencies between your variables. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0700_Reginald 
<<else>>
    Reginald: Thanks to a Smart Variable, I know you cannot afford to bribe me. Alas. #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0800_Reginald 
<<endif>>
Reginald: Farewell! #line:Room6_SmartVariables_1_0900_Reginald 
===

title: Room7_LineGroups_1
group: Room7
position: 947,-227
---
=> Sven: HI FRIEND! #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0100_Sven 
=> Sven: Hi there! I'm Sven. #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0200_Sven 
=> Sven: Welcome! I'm so excited! #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0300_Sven 
Sven: You'll get a different greeting from me depending on which one of my Line Group lines is selected. #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0400_Sven 
Sven: Yarn Spinner will choose one of the lines in a Line Group for you. #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0500_Sven 
Sven: It lets you add some variety. #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0600_Sven 
Sven: You can even add conditions to lines in a line group. #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0700_Sven 
Sven: It's pretty great! #line:Room7_LineGroups_1_0800_Sven 
===

title: Room7_NodeGroups_1
group: Room7
when: once 
when: !visited("Room7_NodeGroups_1")
---
Dr Node: Hi, I'm Doctor Node. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0100_DrNode 
Dr Node: I'm here to show you how Node Groups work. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0200_DrNode 
Dr Node: Node Groups let you create a collection of Nodes that share the same name. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0300_DrNode 
Dr Node: Each Node that's part of the group has a "when" condition in its header... and that when condition dictates when it's shown. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0400_DrNode 
Dr Node: You're seeing these lines because this node in the Node Group has its when condition set to once. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0500_DrNode 
Dr Node: Which means you'll see it once. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0600_DrNode 
Dr Node: Try speaking to me again. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.209d21f6_0700_DrNode 
===

title: Room7_NodeGroups_1
group: Room7
when: !$player_can_afford_bribe
---
Dr Node: Hi. You're seeing this because this node has a when condition that evaluates to true if you cannot afford a bribe. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.786857e8_0100_DrNode 
Dr Node: Neat, right? #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.786857e8_0200_DrNode 
===

title: Room7_NodeGroups_1
group: Room7
when: $player_meal == .None
---
Dr Node: Hi.  #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.975a742d_0100_DrNode 
Dr Node: You haven't got a meal. Alas. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.975a742d_0200_DrNode 
Dr Node: I know this because of my when clause, thanks Node Groups! #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.975a742d_0300_DrNode 
===

title: Room7_NodeGroups_1
group: Room7
when: $player_meal == .Ramen
---
Dr Node: Hi.  #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.405b6843_0100_DrNode 
Dr Node: You have RAMEN! How exciting. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.405b6843_0200_DrNode 
Dr Node: I know this because of my when clause, thanks Node Groups! #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.405b6843_0300_DrNode 
===

title: Room7_NodeGroups_1
group: Room7
when: always
---
Dr Node: Hi. This node in the node group has its when clause set to always. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.2cd2945a_0100_DrNode 
Dr Node: So it's kind of like a fallback. #line:Room7_NodeGroups_1.2cd2945a_0200_DrNode 
===